<title>LEBANON: Lebanese CPI seen up by 7.63 pct Jan-Nov.</title>
<headline>Lebanese CPI seen up by 7.63 pct Jan-Nov.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanese consumer prices rose 7.63 percent in the first 11 months of 1996, according to figures issued on Saturday by the Lebanese Banks Association.</p>
<p>The Association issued the following figures for the Consumer Price Index (Dec 1994 = 100):</p>
<p>		  Dec 95   Sep 96   Oct 96   Nov 96   Dec 95-Nov 96</p>
<p>									  %</p>
<p>		  111.24   123.00   121.58   119.73	  7.63</p>
<p>Monthly</p>
<p>Changes (%)		 1.60    (1.16)   (1.52)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057</p>
</text>
